From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:05:07 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Pinch zoom: send zoom constraints through the window's widget

Every page lives in the parent process here, inside the browser window, so
its root frame has no widget of its own: GetOwnWidget returned null, the
constraints were never sent, and APZ kept its defaults, in which zooming is
not allowed. A pinch began and did nothing on every page. Use the nearest
widget, as Android does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 layout/base/ZoomConstraintsClient.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/layout/base/ZoomConstraintsClient.cpp b/layout/base/ZoomConstraintsClient.cpp
index d243b6b2cb..b3bcf757e5 100644
--- a/layout/base/ZoomConstraintsClient.cpp
+++ b/layout/base/ZoomConstraintsClient.cpp
@@ -51,7 +51,12 @@ static nsIWidget* GetWidget(PresShell* aPresShell) {
     return nullptr;
   }
   if (nsIFrame* rootFrame = aPresShell->GetRootFrame()) {
-#if defined(MOZ_WIDGET_ANDROID)
+    // GECKO_W10M: every page is in the parent process here, inside the browser
+    // window, so its root frame has no widget of its own -- GetOwnWidget was
+    // null, the constraints were never sent, and APZ kept its defaults, in
+    // which zooming is not allowed: a pinch began and did nothing on every
+    // page. The window's widget owns the APZ tree manager, as on Android.
+#if defined(MOZ_WIDGET_ANDROID) || defined(GECKO_W10M)
     // On Android in cases of about:XX pages loaded in the browser parent
     // process we need to return the nearest widget since it's the widget owning
     // an IAPZCTreeManager to communicate with the APZCTreeManager for the
